<p id="mwBA"><b id="mwBQ">Danielle Lynn Dixson</b><sup about="#mwt6" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-phd_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"phd"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-phd-1" id="mwBg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQ">]</span></span></a></sup> is an American ecologist. She was previously an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Associate_professor" title="Associate professor" id="mwCg">Associate Professor</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Marine_ecologist" title="Marine ecologist" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCw">Marine Ecology</a> in the School of Marine Science and Policy at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./University_of_Delaware" title="University of Delaware" id="mwDA">University of Delaware</a>.<sup about="#mwt9" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-2"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-:0-2" id="mwDQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA">]</span></span></a></sup> Her research focusses on how human-induced change to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Marine_ecosystem" title="Marine ecosystem" id="mwEQ">marine ecosystems</a> impacts <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Animal_behaviour" title="Animal behaviour" id="mwEg">animal behaviour</a>.<sup about="#mwt12" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-3" id="mwEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg">]</span></span></a></sup> Her work, now thought to be fraudulent,<sup about="#mwt13" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-:2-4" id="mwFw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">]</span></span></a></sup> was about understanding how <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ocean_acidification" title="Ocean acidification" id="mwGw">ocean acidification</a> affects the behaviour of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Coral_reef" title="Coral reef" id="mwHA">coral reef</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Fish" title="Fish" id="mwHQ">fishes</a>.<sup about="#mwt16" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-5" id="mwHg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIQ">]</span></span></a></sup> As of 2022 her work however came under scrutiny due to inexplicable data. As of August 2026 three of her papers have been retracted <sup about="#mwt19" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-6" id="mwIg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJA">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}' id="mwJg"/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwJw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Academic_career">Academic career</h2>
<p id="mwKA">Dixson studied <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Marine_Science" title="Marine Science" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKQ">Marine Science</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./University_of_Tampa" title="University of Tampa" id="mwKg">University of Tampa</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Florida" title="Florida" id="mwKw">Florida</a>, obtaining her <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Bachelor_of_Science" title="Bachelor of Science" id="mwLA">B.S.</a> in 2005. She went on to obtain her <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ph.D." title="Ph.D." class="mw-redirect" id="mwLQ">Ph.D.</a> in 2012 under the supervision of Philip Munday, Geoffrey Jones, and Morgan Pratchett at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./James_Cook_University" title="James Cook University" id="mwLg">James Cook University</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Australia" title="Australia" id="mwLw">Australia</a>.<sup about="#mwt22" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-phd_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"phd"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-phd-1"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-phd-1" id="mwMA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMw">]</span></span></a></sup> From 2011, she worked as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Postdoctoral_researcher" title="Postdoctoral researcher" id="mwNA">postdoctoral researcher</a> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Georgia_Institute_of_Technology" title="Georgia Institute of Technology" class="mw-redirect" id="mwNQ">Georgia Institute of Technology</a> until her appointment as an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Assistant_professor" title="Assistant professor" id="mwNg">Assistant Professor</a> in 2013.<sup about="#mwt25" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-7" id="mwNw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOQ">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOg">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2015 she began as an assistant professor at the University of Delaware before becoming an associate professor in 2019.<sup about="#mwt26" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_2-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-:0-2" id="mwOw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPg">]</span></span></a></sup> She was fired from the University of Delaware in 2023 due to concerns about fraudulent research.<sup about="#mwt29" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-8" id="mwPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQQ">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwQw">Dixson is the author of Sea Stories, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Children's_literature" title="Children's literature" id="mwRA">children's book</a> series based on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Scientific_literature" title="Scientific literature" id="mwRQ">scientific literature</a> that aims to promote awareness of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Marine_conservation" title="Marine conservation" id="mwRg">marine conservation</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Science,_technology,_engineering,_and_mathematics" title="Science, technology, engineering, and mathematics" id="mwRw">STEM</a> subjects, and visibility of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Minority_group" title="Minority group" id="mwSA">minorities</a> from an early age.<sup about="#mwt32" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-9" id="mwSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">]</span></span></a></sup> She is a member of the International Society of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Chemical_ecology" title="Chemical ecology" id="mwTQ">Chemical Ecology</a> and was the recipient of their Early Career Award in 2019.<sup about="#mwt35" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-10"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-:1-10" id="mwTg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUA">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwUg"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Research">Research</h2>
<p id="mwUw">Dixson's research broadly focuses on the relationship of how marine animals sense their environment and how this influences their decisions.<sup about="#mwt38" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-11" id="mwVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">]</span></span></a></sup> Her major research areas include the role of chemical cues in corals and coral reef fishes, and the influence of ocean acidification on fish behaviour.<sup about="#mwt41" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-12" id="mwWA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWg">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwXA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Misconduct_allegations">Misconduct allegations</h2>
<p id="mwXQ">Dixson has been accused of fabricating primary data by other researchers in the field and is the subject of ongoing institutional investigations.<sup about="#mwt44" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-13"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-13" id="mwXg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYA">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYQ">]</span></span></a></sup> On August 9, 2022, <i id="mwYg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Science_(journal)" title="Science (journal)" id="mwYw">Science</a></i> published a piece announcing that an investigation by the University of Delaware found Dixson guilty of scientific misconduct, including data fabrication and falsification related to her work on coral reef fish behaviour.<sup about="#mwt47" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_4-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-4"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-:2-4" id="mwZA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZw">]</span></span></a></sup> A separate investigation is reportedly being conducted by the Georgia Institute of Technology.<sup about="#mwt48" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_4-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-:2-4" id="mwaA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwaQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwag">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaw">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2022 a first retraction happened for Dixson<sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-14" id="mwbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbg">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">]</span></span></a></sup> The next year; a second paper that Dixson originally published in 2016 was retracted on January 16th, 2023.<sup about="#mwt57" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-15"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-15" id="mwcA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcw">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2026 another paper was retracted due to statistically implausible variance in the data<sup about="#mwt60" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-16"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-16" id="mwdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdg">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mweA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Honours_and_awards">Honours and awards</h2>

<ul id="mweQ"><li id="mweg">International Society of Chemical Ecology Early Career Award<sup about="#mwt61" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_10-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-:1-10" id="mwew"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfQ">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwfw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./National_Science_Foundation" title="National Science Foundation" id="mwgA">National Science Foundation</a> (NSF) Faculty Early Career Development Award<sup about="#mwt64" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-17" id="mwgQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgw">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwhQ">James Cook University Outstanding Alumni Award<sup about="#mwt67" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-18" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-18"}}'><a href="./Danielle_Dixson#cite_note-18" id="mwhg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiA">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwig"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="See_also">See also</h2>
